1
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:11,120
Just try staying away, will you?

2
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone short on cash, come to me.

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,980
I've got none either, so don't worry.

4
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:36,300
white clouds.

6
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:42,740
It'll all work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to me.

8
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,520
I've got none either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,980
Look, even Akaneru is burning.

10
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

11
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,540
You get it, right? I get it, I get it.

12
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,460
Once you understand, save up and follow me.

13
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:02,660
Hey!

14
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:03,760
Gah!

15
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:04,740
Gyaaah!

16
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:09,040
Breaking into a car in broad daylight,
right in front of the police box!

17
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:10,780
You've got some nerve, don't you!

18
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:12,600
N-no, it's not! It's not!

19
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,460
This is my car!

20
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,160
What?

21
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:19,040
The Man Who Locked Up Too Much

22
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,840
So, to keep your car from being stolen,

23
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:28,420
you take off the tires and
drain the gas every time you park?

24
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:29,480
That's right.

25
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:32,020
So you didn't come here to sell tires.

26
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:36,040
With precautions like these,
it's unlikely it'll be stolen,

27
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:39,200
but I don't want to regret
being stingy with the effort.

28
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:42,580
So, what's your business at the police box?

29
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,300
That's right.

30
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:48,280
Actually, there's a suspicious noise coming
from inside a house where no one should be.

31
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:50,080
Akisu?

32
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,680
Where's the house? Is it nearby?

33
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:53,900
It's in 3-chome.

34
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,000
We have to hurry.

35
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,780
Screwdriver and...

36
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,680
This apartment building?

37
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:03,720
Yes, the top floor.

38
00:03:13,180 --> 00:03:14,660
It's the door at the very end.

39
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:28,400
What's with all these keyholes?

40
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:30,040
There are thirty of them.

41
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,700
Thirty?

42
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:35,880
And they're all dimple-key types,
resistant to picking.

43
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:41,020
We even received a commendation from the crime prevention association
as a model crime-proof apartment building.

44
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,180
So you're the owner here?

45
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:45,680
Thanks to you, every unit has sold out.

46
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:49,260
I also own about five more
apartment properties in Tokyo.

47
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:51,060
It won't open.

48
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:54,220
Wrong one. It's this one, this one.

49
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:56,460
Opening this door will take all day!

50
00:03:56,460 --> 00:04:01,960
But I can't imagine anyone getting past
all these security measures to break in.

51
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:03,380
Come on.

52
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:05,180
Just hurry up and open it.

53
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:05,760
Yes.

54
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,060
It's open.

55
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:10,880
Good.

56
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:13,520
What?

57
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,320
Here's the... (the lock)

58
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:23,300
What is this door?

59
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:24,900
It's one meter thick.

60
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,120
Is this a safe or something?

61
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,040
The window...

62
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,760
the glass is undamaged.

63
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,080
That means...

64
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,420
I did it again.

65
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:45,380
I forgot to lock it.

66
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:46,540
Lock

67
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:47,660
forgot.

68
00:04:49,940 --> 00:04:51,900
He shouldn't have been
able to get to the back yet.

69
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:53,640
Senpai, over there!

70
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:53,900
Yeah.

71
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,540
It's them.

72
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:58,320
I'll call for backup now.

73
00:04:58,320 --> 00:04:59,780
I can't wait for that.

74
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:00,600
Ka-no...

75
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,080
Senpai!

76
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,380
Ka...

77
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:22,340
Naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa...

78
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:24,520
Looks like he's a habitual offender.

79
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:28,060
Well, the indoor security
system was also perfect, so...

80
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:31,800
Looks like only this gold
picture frame was stolen.

81
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:33,500
Thank you very much.

82
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:37,440
But despite all that security,

83
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:38,820
for someone to break into an empty room?

84
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:40,860
The facilities are still far from adequate.

85
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:43,360
We need to tighten things up much more.

86
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:46,760
That was just a window we forgot to lock.

87
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:50,160
Ryo-chan, did you change your phone?

88
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:54,420
Yeah, I got it from Mr. Jōmae.
I guess it's kind of a hotline.

89
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:58,980
Senpai, Mr. Jōmae asked us to
provide special security for his home.

90
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:01,640
After what happened, he's probably anxious.

91
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:05,800
Apparently he wants to be able to
reach me right away if anything happens.

92
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:13,620
You haven't made some private deal to get money from him,
have you, Ryo-chan?

93
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:14,500
Wh-what?

94
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:20,460
This is strictly security within our duties as police officers,
right, senpai?

95
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:24,580
Of course. You got a bribe too, didn't you?

96
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:28,420
Protecting the safety of citizens' lives is our job,
after all.

97
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:32,160
Yes, yes, what's the matter?

98
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:35,720
Yes, understood. We'll be right there.

99
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:37,980
What happened?

100
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:41,300
It's an emergency. I'm going out for a bit.

101
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,980
He's definitely getting paid for this,
you know.

102
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,840
It's me. Hurry up and open the door!

103
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:55,160
Understood. I'm opening it now.

104
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:01,100
What do you mean?

105
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:05,660
For security reasons, I've reset
the door to open and close faster.

106
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:06,340
What?

107
00:07:07,980 --> 00:07:09,080
Good, that's it.

108
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:19,440
What is this?

109
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:22,660
This is a sile spray.

110
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:25,280
If a visitor shows suspicious behavior,

111
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:27,920
it's a security system that
activates automatically.

112
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,900
Where's the suspicious behavior?

113
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:32,500
I just leaned against the wall for a second,
you know.

114
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:33,760
Tried a bunch of things.

115
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:40,380
Wh-what?

116
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:44,400
Infrared sensors are strung
throughout the hallway.

117
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:45,760
What?

118
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:49,440
Please use these.

119
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,460
Infrared goggles?

120
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:58,840
It's strung up this much?

121
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:03,157
Damn it,

122
00:08:03,207 --> 00:08:06,900
the only clear space is the ceiling!

123
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:09,840
Did we get through?

124
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:11,820
We did it!

125
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:14,320
Now it's a pitfall trap?!

126
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,520
Suspicious persons will be sent straight to
the Boin-bako in the underground parking lot.

127
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:28,940
Sorry, Ryo-san,
but please start over from the beginning.

128
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:37,780
Honestly,
at this rate no customer could ever get in.

129
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:39,720
There we go.

130
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,980
This door does open normally, right?

131
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:48,020
No, from the outside it won't open
unless you enter the access code.

132
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:49,600
Access code?

133
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:55,200
You have to enter a 26-digit code on the
panel beside the door within 5 seconds.

134
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,000
What?

135
00:08:56,720 --> 00:09:00,000
I'll only say it once,
so Ryo-san, please remember it well.

136
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:08,980
The access code is 635023189544713965282405.

137
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:13,000
Wait, what was that again?

138
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:17,980
635002318954471396…

139
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:20,640
Time's up.

140
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:23,440
Ugh, not this again.

141
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:28,040
Please start over from the beginning.

142
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:33,580
That's the third time now!

143
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:40,140
630231895447139652824059

144
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:42,140
Unlocking now.

145
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,620
Ugh...

146
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:56,540
There can't be any more of these, surely...

147
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,640
Gah! Heat sensors!

148
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:05,860
And lasers!

149
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,780
It's a death trap!

150
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,520
We have to start over again.

151
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,620
I quit!

152
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:27,500
Damn, this way is faster!

153
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:32,440
Ryo-san!

154
00:10:32,810 --> 00:10:33,000
So...

155
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:38,380
Just as expected of Ryotsu-san,
climbing up the outer wall!

156
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:42,820
Still, we should have rigged the outer
walls with electric heating wires too.

157
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:46,000
So, what's this payment business about?

158
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:51,120
Yes, actually, we wanted Ryotsu-san to
take a look at our latest security devices.

159
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:56,740
With this security system, you can see at a
glance whether every lock in the house is secured.

160
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:59,580
The windows are 30-centimeter-thick
bulletproof glass.

161
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,200
They also have auxiliary
locks and sensor alarms.

162
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:07,300
Infrared TV cameras and laser devices are
installed in large numbers on the balcony too.

163
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:10,260
The interior walls are one meter thick.

164
00:11:10,260 --> 00:11:12,460
Even if missiles are fired at it,
it'll be fine.

165
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:18,440
And here, you can view the
monitors for all the TV cameras,

166
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:22,860
and this central control room lets
you control all the security devices.

167
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:28,080
How about it, Ryotsu-san?
With this, security is perfect, right?

168
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:31,200
Is this place the Earth
Defense Force or something?

169
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:37,660
Yes, Ryotsu Security Service.

170
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:41,660
Yes, yes, we'll be right over, yes.

171
00:11:43,780 --> 00:11:45,760
This is the third time today.

172
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:49,960
Ryo-san, sorry,
could you go check the gas main valve?

173
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:54,360
Ryo-san, sorry,
I think I forgot to close B-san's window.

174
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:57,720
Ryo-san, sorry,
I left the laundry hanging out.

175
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:00,800
Ryo-san, sorry, Ryo-san.

176
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,220
Ryo-san.

177
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:06,660
What a worrier.

178
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:10,240
Mr. Jomai calls more than ten times a day,
you know.

179
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:12,500
At this rate, my body won't hold up.

180
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:16,460
They're definitely, absolutely
getting paid for this, aren't they.

181
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:31,920
Seriously, seriously

182
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:34,860
Ryotsu-san, please, I'm begging you, help me

183
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:39,800
What's wrong, at this hour of the night?

184
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:42,020
Ryo-san!

185
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:43,560
Ahahaha!

186
00:12:44,220 --> 00:12:45,820
What's wrong? What happened?

187
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,620
Well, come on, have a drink.

188
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:53,420
Never mind that, I'm asking what happened!

189
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:56,940
I can't sleep,
so I thought I'd have a nightcap.

190
00:12:56,940 --> 00:12:57,560
What?

191
00:12:58,640 --> 00:12:59,420
Cheers!

192
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:02,720
Mmmm! Don't mess with me!

193
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:03,320
Ugh.

194
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,100
You're the one who,

195
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:06,980
on the phone, cried, "Please help me!"

196
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:08,980
making it sound like you were about to die,

197
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:11,480
so I rushed right over!

198
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:14,700
And now it's
"I can't sleep, keep me company while I drink"?

199
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,520
S-sorry.

200
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:20,220
When I'm alone at night,
I somehow get terribly lonely,

201
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:21,120
Alone?

202
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:23,800
Then what's this photo?

203
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:26,640
You have a family, don't you? A family!

204
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:28,860
My wife and child have left.

205
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:39,080
It was last summer.

206
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:43,500
I bought my son a bicycle
for his 10th birthday.

207
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:47,120
He practiced every single day,
working hard at it.

208
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:50,060
And just when he had finally
learned to ride it on his own,

209
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:54,740
that bicycle was stolen.

210
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:56,800
Did you give them a theft report?

211
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:57,520
Yes.

212
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:00,840
But in the end, it was never found.

213
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:03,400
The day I saw my son's tears,

214
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:04,980
I made up my mind.

215
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,920
Thieves will never
disappear from this world.

216
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:11,700
So I resolved to protect
my family with my own hands.

217
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:17,320
So you've started locking up absolutely everything,
have you?

218
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:18,120
Yes.

219
00:14:19,220 --> 00:14:22,140
But this is a bit excessive, isn't it?

220
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:23,920
My wife said the same thing.

221
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:28,220
My wife and I often ended
up arguing about the locks,

222
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:33,140
and one day she said she couldn't stand
living in a house full of locks anymore.

223
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:35,560
She left, taking our son with her.

224
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:40,020
So that's why you're living
alone in this big apartment.

225
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:40,660
Yes.

226
00:14:41,060 --> 00:14:43,780
Well, I can understand how
lonely it must be to be alone.

227
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:47,300
But, you know,
what the wife said makes sense.

228
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:51,340
Not to brag, but I've never once
locked my house up until now.

229
00:14:51,340 --> 00:14:54,260
Aren't you worried, though?

230
00:14:54,940 --> 00:14:56,900
Jane, Jane's Jane.

231
00:14:57,280 --> 00:15:01,220
Back when we were kids,
no house ever had its doors locked.

232
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:04,160
So the neighbors could
come and go as they pleased.

233
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:07,400
That's because it was a peaceful era.

234
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:10,600
These days, without locks,
you feel so anxious, so anxious.

235
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:16,520
W-what's this chain?

236
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:19,840
A-a thief!

237
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:20,760
Damn it.

238
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,060
You bastard!

239
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:25,920
What?

240
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:28,780
Because of you, we've ended up with
the worst possible outcome, haven't we?

241
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,840
W-what is this apartment?

242
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:49,440
Forgetting to close the bathroom window,
of all things!

243
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:51,920
How careless of me.

244
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:54,160
Well, it's a good thing I was here.

245
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:56,640
It still can't be called safe.

246
00:15:57,740 --> 00:15:59,880
This won't do. It can't go on like this.

247
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:03,380
We need much, much stricter security.

248
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:07,500
Hey, is Naoko Komachi here?

249
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:09,380
What is it, caveman?

250
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:11,200
What do you want with us?

251
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:13,920
Actually, I have a favor to ask you.

252
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:17,440
Speaking of which, senior...

253
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:21,280
Shiromae hasn't called us
out at all lately, has he?

254
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:23,400
I wonder what's going on with him.

255
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:26,320
Maybe he's finally settled down by now.

256
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:27,780
No, that's unlikely.

257
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:31,540
I don't think that guy
would settle down that easily.

258
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:35,120
Speak of the devil.

259
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:37,640
Yes, Ryotsu Security Service.

260
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,800
What, he moved?

261
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:51,160
It should be somewhere around here, I think.

262
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:59,780
I came to the address I was given,
but there's no house here!

263
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:03,000
An antenna, in a place like this?

264
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:06,180
Hey, there's a keyhole lying over here!

265
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:09,760
This can't be...

266
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:18,500
Ryotsu-san,
I was just about to go out and pick you up.

267
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:20,940
So this is the place you moved to?

268
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:24,220
Yes, it's an underground
shelter developed by NASA.

269
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:26,180
I sold off all my apartments,

270
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:28,500
and put my entire fortune into this.

271
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:31,020
Here, there's only one entrance and exit,

272
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:32,840
and there's no forgetting
to close the windows.

273
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:36,500
I thought it would be ideal
for someone careless like me.

274
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,280
But underground

275
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:41,640
You still lock the door, though?

276
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:44,060
A home without locks makes me anxious.

277
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:54,860
What do you think, Mr. Ryotsu?

278
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:57,920
If you notice anything concerning about security,
please tell me.

279
00:17:57,920 --> 00:18:00,080
I'd like to make improvements.

280
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:03,500
True, with no windows, it's hard for
burglars to get into an empty unit.

281
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:06,500
All the furniture is locked down,
so nothing can be carried off.

282
00:18:07,060 --> 00:18:09,080
It's a home that's a model of safety.

283
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:13,160
But doesn't living in a
place like this feel stifling?

284
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:18,580
Safety comes first,
so that's no big problem at all.

285
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:35,920
Heavy rain that began falling over the Kanto
region is causing widespread damage in many areas.

286
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:41,380
According to the Japan Meteorological Agency,
southern Kanto has seen over 500 millimeters of rain per hour,

287
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:45,000
and the number of houses flooded above
and below floor level has reached 500.

288
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,720
Well, if you're fine with it, I don't mind.

289
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:53,680
If it were me, no matter how safe it was or how much money I was paid,
I'd never want to live in this house.

290
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:58,500
Why? Are there still some flaws?
Please tell me anything you want.

291
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,220
That's not what I mean.

292
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:07,160
I'm talking about whether this is fit
to be a house for people to live in.

293
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,600
Above all, safety comes first in a house.

294
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:15,340
In other words, a house is like a fortress
to protect yourself from enemies, right?

295
00:19:15,340 --> 00:19:18,500
As for me, a house is enough as
long as it keeps the rain off.

296
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:20,580
It's the 21st century, you know.

297
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:23,780
I think that way of
thinking should be changed.

298
00:19:25,918 --> 00:19:30,160
I don't remember asking you to lecture me!
I'm going home!

299
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:34,300
Please wait.

300
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:38,940
There are still various security
devices I want Ryo-san to take a look at.

301
00:19:38,940 --> 00:19:43,100
Relax! No thief can get into this house!

302
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:48,660
What is this? This door is incredibly tough!

303
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:52,000
Nngh... grr... you bastard!

304
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:56,080
It's turned into a sea!

305
00:19:57,260 --> 00:19:58,700
Ryo-san, hurry up, come on!

306
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,120
I know! I know, but with the water pressure,
it's hard to get the door...

307
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:05,400
This place is dangerous! Let's get outside!

308
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:08,860
I can't just abandon my house like that!

309
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:11,460
Let's go!
Which matters more, the house or your life!

310
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,620
What is this?

311
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:29,560
Run!

312
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,760
My home is

313
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:46,360
My home is

314
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:01,760
Everything has been lost.

315
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:05,860
What am I supposed to do now?

316
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:08,200
What did you lose, exactly?

317
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:11,100
That's why it's everything to me.

318
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:12,280
Everything?

319
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:15,460
It's just one house gone, isn't it?

320
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:19,700
Anyway, what is it that you want to protect?

321
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:22,620
What are you locking
your house up to protect?

322
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:24,900
That's...

323
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:28,040
You're locking up an empty treasure chest.

324
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,740
Dad

325
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:49,180
Shinya

326
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:51,020
Sakiko

327
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:53,480
What on earth is going on?

328
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:58,440
His wife and son came to see us,
worried about Mr. Jomae.

329
00:21:58,980 --> 00:22:01,260
Shinya, were you doing okay?

330
00:22:02,060 --> 00:22:03,520
Yeah. Where's Dad?

331
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:09,760
Shinya says he gets lonely without Dad.

332
00:22:10,900 --> 00:22:11,700
I see.

333
00:22:18,020 --> 00:22:19,880
There you are, Kankichi Ryotsu.

334
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:23,120
The bicycle you asked me to look for,
I found it.

335
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:24,320
Found it!

336
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:26,080
Bicycle?

337
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:29,080
This is the bicycle
you're looking for, right?

338
00:22:29,380 --> 00:22:30,500
This bicycle?

339
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:32,480
Jomae Shinya-kun

340
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:33,180
Yes.

341
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,060
It's your bicycle.

342
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:37,980
My bicycle.

343
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:39,680
Not bad.

344
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:40,940
Of course, right?

345
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:42,840
Don't underestimate the Traffic Division.

346
00:22:43,340 --> 00:22:44,200
Ryotsu-san

347
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:47,240
Thank you so much for this time.

348
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:52,280
From now on, the three of us will work
together as a family and start over.

349
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:57,380
Don't lock things up
so much next time, okay?

350
00:22:58,780 --> 00:22:59,140
Yes.

351
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:04,380
About that reward we talked about...

352
00:23:05,380 --> 00:23:08,960
the house I poured my entire
fortune into has been swept away.

353
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:11,260
Hey, what are we supposed to do now?

354
00:23:11,260 --> 00:23:14,640
You said my reward was 50,000 yen per visit!

355
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:17,500
You called me out ten,
even twenty times a day!

356
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:18,760
So that's how it is.

357
00:23:18,760 --> 00:23:20,280
Senpai.

358
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:23,660
You didn't make some private deal to take money from him,
did you?

359
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:24,800
You didn't, right?

360
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:29,980
You were only guarding him within the scope
of your duties as police officers, right?

361
00:23:29,980 --> 00:23:31,360
That's right, that's right.

362
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:34,080
I didn't make any
promise to get paid at all.

363
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:35,040
W-well

364
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:35,620
Y-yes.

365
00:23:35,620 --> 00:23:37,540
By the way, Ryotsu Kankichi.

366
00:23:37,540 --> 00:23:41,400
You promised to treat us to top-grade sushi if we found the bicycle,
didn't you?

367
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:41,800
Gulp.

368
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:46,700
Since we specially asked 300 traffic officers
across the whole Kanto region to help.

369
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:49,520
So, 300 servings of top-grade sushi, please.

370
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:50,760
300 servings?

371
00:23:53,900 --> 00:23:57,120
I've lost everything too.

372
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:58,240
What are you talking about?

373
00:23:58,240 --> 00:24:02,260
You're definitely going to treat us to 300 servings of top-grade sushi,
you hear?

374
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:27,460
I probably don't want to become
someone who goes all-out in dumb games.

375
00:24:28,020 --> 00:24:32,040
If you let your road rot at the corner,

376
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:34,400
the moon has run away.

377
00:24:35,380 --> 00:24:38,160
Because now isn't everything.

378
00:24:39,280 --> 00:24:42,700
Don't push yourself too hard.

379
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:46,340
Even if you fudge things a little,

380
00:24:47,160 --> 00:24:50,520
sometimes you're helping someone.

381
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:56,860
You know me,
heading toward tomorrow with a nice spirit.

382
00:24:58,040 --> 00:25:04,340
I won't rot,
I'll do what needs doing, a cute spirit.

383
00:25:04,340 --> 00:25:11,540
It's hard to understand
because I want to look that way.

384
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:17,300
Better than a makeover
that's all show, right?

385
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:24,860
Na na na na na na na na na na na na na.

386
00:25:47,300 --> 00:25:47,700
Nice to meet you!

